# @aegis/website
# Copy to `.env.local`. Never commit a filled-in copy.

# ── Public — inlined into the browser bundle. Nothing secret may ever live here.

# The site's own origin. Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, the sitemap
# and robots.txt. Left at the default in production, every canonical URL points
# at localhost — and search engines will act on that.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3100"

NEXT_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT="development"

# Where the "Get started" gateway sends each audience. These are separate
# applications on separate origins, not routes inside this one — see the note in
# `src/lib/site.ts` for why that split is deliberate.
#
# The customer portal points at the live `frontend/` app today. It must stay on
# port 3000 in development: the Google sign-in origin is registered against it
# (see frontend/PORT.md).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CUSTOMER_PORTAL_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMPLOYEE_PORTAL_URL="http://localhost:3102"
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENTERPRISE_PORTAL_URL="http://localhost:3103"
NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_ADMIN_URL="http://localhost:3104"

# ── Server-only. Readable in route handlers, never shipped to the browser.

# Where contact and demo enquiries are delivered. Unset, the route handler still
# validates and throttles, then writes the enquiry to the server log with a
# warning — recoverable, but nobody is notified. Point this at a CRM intake, an
# email service or an automation webhook before launch.
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=""
